eah  do you have friends um yes i'm friends  with the girls that are in my soaker  house i didn't really have friends in  high school  just because i was very shy and  didn't really know how to talk to people  about being so uncomfortable in your own  body  so i do have some really nice friends um  in sober living  what is you know you're only 23 but what  what lessons have you learned  you know from living you've been you've  been on the street for how long  um on and off for five years mostly on  yeah and you've been treated badly and  it sounds like sometimes what what  lessons have you learned  about others about people to never give  up  as much as it seems like it's never  going to get better  like after all the stuff that i've gone  through and  i thought it would never ever end but  there's always at some point it will end  and it will get better and you can have  a happy and fulfilling life  do you find your family is helpful or  supportive at this point um they're  giving you money which is good  um my siblings are really supportive my  younger sister  she's a lesbian and she's very  supportive my older  sister and older brother he's very  supportive the only people that aren't  really that supportive are my parents  they tolerate it but they don't accept  it  like they won't even talk about it with  me  but i kind of i don't let that bother me  though because you know what just  they don't have to you know accept me as  long as i  accept me exactly  it's across the board for everybody i  think yeah  awesome well gwendolyn thank you so much  for sharing your story yeah thank you  very very interesting talking with you  thank you  you

